  "difficulty": "Intermediate",
  "domain": "Food Delivery",
  "statement": "In an on-demand food delivery platform, a Customer can Browse Restaurants and Place Order. Placing an order always requires Process Payment via an external Payment Gateway. Optionally, the Customer may Apply Promo Code while placing an order. A Courier can Accept Delivery and Update Delivery Status, while a Restaurant Partner can Confirm Order Preparation.",
  "deliverables": [
    "Model all four actors (Customer, Courier, Restaurant Partner, Payment Gateway).",
    "Capture browsing, ordering, payment processing, promo codes, delivery acceptance, status updates, and order confirmation.",
    "Distinguish mandatory «include» behavior from optional «extend» behavior."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Place Order «include»s Process Payment, and Process Payment associates with the secondary Payment Gateway actor.",
    "Apply Promo Code is optional, so it «extend»s Place Order.",
    "Group Courier actions (Accept Delivery, Update Delivery Status) and Restaurant Partner actions cleanly."
  ],
